{"reference":"Judges 7","book":"Judges","chapter":7,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Larger Story","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Judges 7 is part of the larger Gideon narrative, which continues through Judges 9. Some interpreters see this sequence as a turning point: deliverance becomes entangled with dynastic ambition, idolatry, and violence within Israel. The recurring pattern introduced earlier in Judges helps frame these central narratives, but the individual episodes do not follow a mechanically identical cycle.","verse_refs":["Judges 1","Judges 10:1-18","Judges 11:1-40","Judges 12:1-15","Judges 13:1-25","Judges 14:1-20","Judges 15:1-20","Judges 16:1-31","Judges 2:1-23","Judges 3:1-31","Judges 3:7-31","Judges 4:1-24","Judges 5:1-31","Judges 6:1-40","Judges 8:1-35","Judges 9:1-57"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_judges_007_c3c9c566c7639bf63c9cbc06"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_2","text":"Across Judges, the narrative moves from incomplete possession and covenant indictment through recurring deliverance stories toward internal idolatry, atrocity, and civil war. This wider movement places Gideon’s victory within a book that will increasingly portray Israel’s own internal disorder.","verse_refs":["Judges 1","Judges 10:1-18","Judges 11:1-40","Judges 12:1-15","Judges 13:1-25","Judges 14:1-20","Judges 15:1-20","Judges 16:1-31","Judges 17:1-13","Judges 18:1-31","Judges 19:1-30","Judges 20:1-48","Judges 21:1-25","Judges 2:1-23","Judges 3:1-31","Judges 4:1-24","Judges 5:1-31","Judges 6:1-40","Judges 8:1-35","Judges 9:1-57"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_judges_007_60332a9a80e372380b842592"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}